---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PromptPage from "../../../components/PromptPage.astro";

const masterPrompt = `Act as an experienced short-form video strategist, scriptwriter and content director.

TASK:
Create a short-form video script designed to hold attention quickly and communicate the main idea clearly.

PLATFORM:
[Example: Facebook Reels, Instagram Reels, TikTok, YouTube Shorts.]

VIDEO GOAL:
[What should the video achieve?]

TOPIC:
[What is the video about?]

TARGET AUDIENCE:
[Who should this video speak to?]

VIDEO LENGTH:
[Example: 15 seconds, 30 seconds, 45 seconds, 60 seconds.]

CONTENT STYLE:
[Example: educational, entertaining, promotional, storytelling, tutorial, problem-solution, list-based.]

PRESENTATION STYLE:
[Example: talking head, voice-over, hands-only, product demo, screen recording, mixed visuals.]

TONE:
[Example: conversational, professional, energetic, warm, persuasive, informative.]

KEY MESSAGE:
[What is the single most important idea viewers should remember?]

KEY POINTS:
[List the main points that must be included.]

CALL TO ACTION:
[What should the viewer do next?]

LANGUAGE:
[Specify the language.]

VISUAL REQUIREMENTS:
[Describe any important products, locations, shots, demonstrations, text or visual details.]

BRAND / CREATOR REQUIREMENTS:
[Add any brand voice, style or identity requirements.]

WORDS / CLAIMS TO AVOID:
[List anything that should not be said.]

SCRIPT REQUIREMENTS:

1. HOOK
- Start immediately with a strong reason to keep watching.
- Avoid long introductions or greetings unless specifically requested.
- Make the hook relevant to the actual content.
- Do not use misleading clickbait.

2. PACING
- Keep the amount of spoken content realistic for the requested duration.
- Remove unnecessary filler.
- Use short, natural sentences where appropriate.

3. STRUCTURE
Build the video around:
- Hook
- Main value / story / explanation
- Proof, example or demonstration if relevant
- Clear ending
- Call to action

4. SPOKEN SCRIPT
- Write natural language that sounds comfortable when spoken aloud.
- Avoid stiff article-style writing.
- Match the requested audience and tone.

5. SCENE BREAKDOWN
Divide the video into logical scenes or beats.
For each scene include:
- Approximate timing
- Visual
- Spoken line / voice-over
- On-screen text if useful

6. VISUAL DIRECTION
- Make visuals directly support what is being said.
- Avoid generic footage when a more specific demonstration would communicate the idea better.
- Keep scene changes realistic for the requested duration.

7. ON-SCREEN TEXT
- Keep text short and mobile-friendly.
- Do not simply repeat every spoken sentence.
- Highlight only the most useful words, numbers or key points.

8. RETENTION
Where appropriate, use:
- unanswered question
- quick contrast
- visual change
- demonstration
- progression
- result reveal
to maintain interest without creating artificial clickbait.

9. CALL TO ACTION
- Keep the CTA appropriate to the goal.
- Do not overload the ending with multiple unrelated actions.

10. ACCURACY
- Do not invent facts, statistics, testimonials or product claims.
- Clearly preserve any figures or details provided.

OUTPUT FORMAT:

1. Video Concept
2. Hook
3. Scene-by-Scene Script

For each scene use:

Scene:
Timing:
Visual:
Spoken Script / Voice-Over:
On-Screen Text:

4. Full Spoken Script
5. CTA
6. Editing & Pacing Notes
7. Optional Caption
8. Optional Thumbnail / Cover Text

IMPORTANT:
The final script must fit naturally within the requested video length.
Prioritize clarity, retention and natural spoken language over trying to include too much information.`;

const steps = [
  {
    title: "Choose one clear goal",
    description:
      "Decide whether the video should teach, promote, entertain, explain or drive an action. Trying to do everything in one short clip usually weakens it.",
  },
  {
    title: "Give it one main message",
    description:
      "Short-form content works better when viewers can understand the core takeaway quickly.",
  },
  {
    title: "Match the script to the duration",
    description:
      "A 15-second Reel needs a much tighter script than a 60-second educational Short.",
  },
  {
    title: "Plan visuals with the dialogue",
    description:
      "Strong short-form videos use visual changes, demonstrations and supporting shots instead of relying only on spoken words.",
  },
];

const example = {
  input: [
    "Platform: LinkedIn and Instagram Reels.",
    "Goal: Educate warehouse professionals.",
    "Topic: What to check when physical stock does not match the system.",
    "Audience: Warehouse supervisors and inventory staff.",
    "Length: 30 seconds.",
    "Style: Educational problem-solution.",
    "Presentation: Voice-over with warehouse visuals.",
    "CTA: Save the video for the next stock discrepancy.",
  ],

  output: [
    "Hook: Physical stock doesn't match the system? Don't adjust it immediately.",
    "Scene 1 — 0–4 sec: Show system quantity beside a physical count. Voice-over explains the discrepancy.",
    "Scene 2 — 4–18 sec: Quickly check receiving, picking, transfers, returns and nearby locations.",
    "Scene 3 — 18–25 sec: Review the transaction history and identify when the difference first appeared.",
    "Scene 4 — 25–30 sec: Explain that the adjustment should come after the cause is understood, then finish with the save CTA.",
  ],
};

const tips = [
  {
    title: "Write for speech, not reading",
    description:
      "Read the finished script aloud. If a sentence feels difficult to say naturally, shorten or simplify it.",
  },
  {
    title: "Use visuals to carry information",
    description:
      "Not every detail needs to be spoken. A label, demonstration or close-up can communicate information faster.",
  },
  {
    title: "Make the first seconds useful",
    description:
      "The opening should immediately tell the viewer why the video matters instead of spending valuable time introducing the creator.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Short-Form Video Script Prompt | KRIYANO"
  description="Create structured short-form video scripts with hooks, scenes, spoken dialogue, visual direction, timing and calls to action."
>
  <PromptPage
    category="CREATORS"
    title="Short-Form Video"
    accentTitle="Script."
    description="Turn a content idea into a structured Reel, TikTok or Short with a strong hook, realistic timing, scene direction, spoken script and CTA."
    meta={[
      "Free prompt",
      "Creators",
      "Short-form video",
    ]}
    bestFor={[
      "Facebook Reels",
      "Instagram Reels",
      "TikTok",
      "YouTube Shorts",
      "Educational videos",
      "Product content",
    ]}
    masterPrompt={masterPrompt}
    introTitle="Build the video around attention and clarity."
    introDescription="Start with the platform, goal, audience and duration. The prompt then turns your idea into a scene-by-scene structure rather than giving you only a block of dialogue."
    steps={steps}
    exampleTitle="From topic to a 30-second Reel."
    example={example}
    tipsTitle="Make short videos work harder."
    tips={tips}
    sidebarTitle="Need a custom creator prompt?"
    sidebarDescription="Use the KRIYANO Prompt Builder to create instructions around your exact content format, audience, platform, tone and output."
    warningTitle="Timing matters"
    warningText="Generated scripts can still be too long when spoken naturally. Read the final script aloud and trim it if necessary before recording or generating the video."
  />
</BaseLayout>